\subsection{Next-Gen Component ABIs: Zircon \& \OpenHarmony}
\label{sec:nextgen_abis}

In addition to legacy monolithic ABIs, Telix natively supports modern
component-oriented architectures:

\begin{description}
    \item[\textbf{Fuchsia / Zircon ABI}] \footcite{fuchsia_zircon}: Zircon relies on Object Handles and Channel Message passing (FIDL). Because Telix's native capability model is structurally isomorphic to Zircon handles, Zircon syscalls exhibit near 1:1 translation efficiency into native Telix capability channels.

    \item[\textbf{\OpenHarmony\ Subsystem}] \footcite{openharmony23}: \OpenHarmony\ services communicate via Binder IPC. Telix emulates Binder interfaces using lock-free shared memory rings, allowing \OpenHarmony\ components to run transparently across Telix multikernel partitions.
\end{description}
